   ],
   "id": "ch03_03"
  },
  {
   "narration": "People hid in car boots, used forged passports, and once even slid across on a homemade zip line. In 1979, two families escaped East Germany in a hot air balloon sewn together from scraps of fabric.",
   "background": {
    "type": "footage",
    "image_id": 736879,
